Tanning is the ranger's art of treating raw hides and skins to create
usable leather. After skinning an animal, the raw hide must be properly
tanned before it can be worked into clothing, armor, or other goods.

To tan a hide, you must have access to the proper materials and workspace.
The tanning process takes time and skill - poorly tanned leather will be
of lesser quality and value than that produced by a master tanner.

Higher skill in tanning produces better quality leather from the same raw
materials. Expert tanners can sometimes coax exceptional results from
ordinary hides, while novices may ruin valuable skins.

